Diagnose a second module loaded from source at a path the session already holds a module for.

Linkage::loadModuleFromBlob (source/slang/slang-session.cpp), behind loadModuleFromSource and
loadModuleFromSourceString, returns the cached module when its name is already loaded and diagnoses
E38202 when that name was loaded from different source. A module under a new name at a path that
another module was loaded from goes on to Linkage::loadParsedModule, which adds it to
mapPathToLoadedModule under the path's most unique identity:

    mapPathToLoadedModule.add(mostUniqueIdentity, loadedModule);   // 1261

Dictionary::add asserts on a key that is already present (source/core/slang-dictionary.h:322-325),
so the second load returns null with "assert failure: slang-dictionary.h(325): The key already
exists in Dictionary." as its only diagnostic text and no diagnostic code.

This checks the path before loading and diagnoses a new error, E38208 module-path-already-loaded,
naming the path and the module, and returns null as the other refusals in loadModuleFromBlob do. A
module at a new path, and a module whose name is already loaded, take the same path as before. A
regression test is added as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-module-path-already-loaded.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21: before, null with the assert text and no code (win-x64); after, null with
E38208 naming 'shared.slang'.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua b/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua
index b94f1344f..1d7fa801b 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua
+++ b/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua
@@ -4959,6 +4959,13 @@ err(
     span { loc = "location", message = "a module named '~moduleName:Name' is already loaded from different source contents in this session. Use a different module name or drop references to the previous module before reloading." }
 )
 
+err(
+    "module-path-already-loaded",
+    38208,
+    "a module is already loaded from path '~path'",
+    span { loc = "location", message = "a module is already loaded from path '~path' in this session, so module '~moduleName:Name' cannot be loaded from it. Use a different path for each module loaded from source." }
+)
+
 -- Note: compilationCeased is a fatal diagnostic that is locationless
 fatal(
     "compilation-ceased",
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-session.cpp b/source/slang/slang-session.cpp
index a7931f933..9141ac443 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-session.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-session.cpp
@@ -447,6 +447,19 @@ slang::IModule* Linkage::loadModuleFromBlob(
                 pathInfo = PathInfo::makeNormal(pathStr, cannonicalPath);
             }
         }
+        // A second module under another name at a path the session already holds a module for would
+        // be added to `mapPathToLoadedModule` under the same key, so it is diagnosed here instead.
+        //
+        if (mapPathToLoadedModule.containsKey(pathInfo.getMostUniqueIdentity()))
+        {
+            sink.diagnose(Diagnostics::ModulePathAlreadyLoaded{
+                .path = pathStr,
+                .moduleName = name,
+                .location = SourceLoc(),
+            });
+            sink.getBlobIfNeeded(outDiagnostics);
+            return nullptr;
+        }
         RefPtr<Module> module =
             loadModuleImpl(name, pathInfo, sourceBlob, SourceLoc(), &sink, nullptr, blobType);
         if (module)
